y","/arc-plc/south-carolina/oconee-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids July to August and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 35 years. In 2025, November to December came in at 32% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 42% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2016, with grid 17289 down to 56% that year.</p>"}
